<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>IRC channel logs</title><style>html {
  background: #fdfdfd;
}

h1 {
  font-weight: 300;
}

h2 {
  font-weight: 200;
}

h3 {
  padding: .5em 0;
  border-top: 3px dotted #ddd;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

form {
  width: 400px;
  display: flex;
}

input {
  width: 100%;
  display: flex;
  border-radius: .25em 0 0 .25em;
  border: 1px solid #aaa;
  border-right: 0;
  padding: 0.5em;
}

button {
  display: flex;
  border-radius: 0 .25em .25em 0;
  background-color: #007bff;
  border: 1px solid #007bff;
  padding: .5em;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: white;
}

button:hover {
  background-color: #0069d9;
  border-color: #0062cc;
}

a {
  color: #007bff;
  text-decoration: none;
}

a:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}

h4 {
  margin-bottom: .5em;
}

table td {
  padding: 0.75em;
}

table tr:hover {
  background: #eee;
}

.year {
  display: table;
}

.month {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-right: 1em;
}

ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.nick {
  padding-right: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-align: right;
  width: 13rem;
  display: table-cell;
}

.nick a {
  color: inherit;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.message {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-left: 0.6rem;
  border-left: 2px solid #333;
}

.notice {
  color: #859900;
  font-style: italic;
}

.line {
  line-height: 1.8rem;
  display: table;
}

#logs {
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-10-24.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="005249"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005249" label="[00:52:49]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">nope, musl libc.so dynamic loader still errors with &quot;illegal instruction&quot;, when compiled with tcc</span></div><div class="line" id="005319"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005319" label="[00:53:19]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">no big deal yet, because i hacked full static linking support into my system profile for i486-tcc-linux-musl</span></div><div class="line" id="005338"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#005338" label="[00:53:38]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">however, then i can't keep perl/autotools for system integration, which is a whole other debate</span></div><div class="line" id="021145"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#021145" label="[02:11:45]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">strangely, when musl-libc is compiled/linked with gcc then $ file libc.so # dynamic loader identifies as &quot;LSB shared object .. dynamically linked&quot;</span></div><div class="line" id="021224"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#021224" label="[02:12:24]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">when compiled/linked with CC|LD=i386-tcc then $file libc.so identifies as &quot;LSB shared object .. static-pie linked&quot;</span></div><div class="line" id="021307"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#021307" label="[02:13:07]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">no clue where the static-pie linked comes from, i think tcc handles this differently, when stuffing together ELF sections</span></div><div class="line" id="021344"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#021344" label="[02:13:44]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and although the _dlstart entry point of libc.so matches the adress, when executing ./libc.so &quot;illegal instruction&quot; is reported</span></div><div class="line" id="021345"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#021345" label="[02:13:45]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">weird</span></div><div class="line" id="021521"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#021521" label="[02:15:21]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">as a consequence, when musl-libc is compiled/linked with tcc, it can't support dynamic loading of shared objects</span></div><div class="line" id="021548"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#021548" label="[02:15:48]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">hence, i can't keep Perl/autotools, for example, because it needs dynamic loading</span></div><div class="line" id="021722"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#021722" label="[02:17:22]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">perl should work statically</span></div><div class="line" id="021802"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#021802" label="[02:18:02]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ok, that's my main concern here, because i can live with static-linking</span></div><div class="line" id="021819"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#021819" label="[02:18:19]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">but i failed to emit a fully working perl interpreter that is needed for autotools/automake</span></div><div class="line" id="021938"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#021938" label="[02:19:38]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">stikonas: there's some hackjob floating on the internet, to support static-linking of perl, but that's much hazzle</span></div><div class="line" id="022006"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022006" label="[02:20:06]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">you could always take a look at live-bootstra</span></div><div class="line" id="022012"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022012" label="[02:20:12]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">we did get perl statically linked</span></div><div class="line" id="022029"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022029" label="[02:20:29]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">feel free  to borrow build scripts from there</span></div><div class="line" id="022034"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#022034" label="[02:20:34]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">stikonas: i too got it, but it failed to support some extras needed by autotools/automake</span></div><div class="line" id="022046"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#022046" label="[02:20:46]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">question, could you confirm autotools/automake/autoreconf?</span></div><div class="line" id="022058"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022058" label="[02:20:58]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I think mostly old ones</span></div><div class="line" id="022102"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022102" label="[02:21:02]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">definitely not the latest</span></div><div class="line" id="022105"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022105" label="[02:21:05]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">let me check</span></div><div class="line" id="022159"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#022159" label="[02:21:59]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">i tested with perl-6.8.6 and automake-1.15.1 iirc</span></div><div class="line" id="022211"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#022211" label="[02:22:11]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">*5.8.6</span></div><div class="line" id="022236"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022236" label="[02:22:36]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">automake 2.15.1  and autoconf 2.69</span></div><div class="line" id="022243"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022243" label="[02:22:43]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">1.15.1</span></div><div class="line" id="022245"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022245" label="[02:22:45]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yes</span></div><div class="line" id="022255"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022255" label="[02:22:55]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and perl 5.6.2 worked</span></div><div class="line" id="022300"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#022300" label="[02:23:00]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">with a statically linked perl interpreter? this would be awesome stikonas !</span></div><div class="line" id="022302"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022302" label="[02:23:02]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">haven't tried 5.8</span></div><div class="line" id="022304"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022304" label="[02:23:04]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yes</span></div><div class="line" id="022309"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#022309" label="[02:23:09]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ok, good enough</span></div><div class="line" id="022313"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022313" label="[02:23:13]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message"> <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/fosslinux/live-bootstrap/blob/master/parts.rst">https://github.com/fosslinux/live-bootstrap/blob/master/parts.rst</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="022324"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022324" label="[02:23:24]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">there is no dynamic linking here till much later</span></div><div class="line" id="022400"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#022400" label="[02:24:00]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">have you tried to spawn an autoreconf with any project?</span></div><div class="line" id="022401"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022401" label="[02:24:01]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">we have used these steps to build perl <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/fosslinux/live-bootstrap/blob/master/steps/perl-5.6.2/mk/main.mk">https://github.com/fosslinux/live-bootstrap/blob/master/steps/perl-5.6.2/mk/main.mk</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="022407"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022407" label="[02:24:07]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yes, almost surely</span></div><div class="line" id="022413"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#022413" label="[02:24:13]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ok</span></div><div class="line" id="022451"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#022451" label="[02:24:51]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">good, i just tried the latest perl-version that tcc could digest; but perl-5.6 is fine if that is known to work</span></div><div class="line" id="022452"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022452" label="[02:24:52]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">see that build script</span></div><div class="line" id="022455"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#022455" label="[02:24:55]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">thanks!</span></div><div class="line" id="022457"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022457" label="[02:24:57]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">you might have been missing some perl modules</span></div><div class="line" id="022505"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022505" label="[02:25:05]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">they can be build statically into it</span></div><div class="line" id="022539"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022539" label="[02:25:39]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">in particular here <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/fosslinux/live-bootstrap/blob/master/steps/perl-5.6.2/mk/main.mk#L115">https://github.com/fosslinux/live-bootstrap/blob/master/steps/perl-5.6.2/mk/main.mk#L115</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="022556"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022556" label="[02:25:56]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">there are various extra extensions that are then built into perl statically</span></div><div class="line" id="022601"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#022601" label="[02:26:01]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I guess normally those are dynamic</span></div><div class="line" id="032633"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#032633" label="[03:26:33]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Googulator: thinking further on your UART question; if we use hardware flow control and if the builder-hex0 kernel stalls if the uart buffer is full, until it has capacity. Any speed would be acceptable (just slower speed terminals wouls significantly slow down the total process)</span></div><div class="line" id="032738"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#032738" label="[03:27:38]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">(There should be some good discrete 8bit UARTs that should meet that requirement)</span></div><div class="line" id="224027"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#224027" label="[22:40:27]">&lt;qbit&gt;</a></span><span class="message">hi!</span></div><div class="line" id="232852"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#232852" label="[23:28:52]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">qbit: hi</span></div><div class="line" id="233859"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#233859" label="[23:38:59]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">fossy: looks like we again have some openssl trouble...</span></div><div class="line" id="233905"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#233905" label="[23:39:05]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message"> <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/fosslinux/live-bootstrap/actions/runs/11507728726/job/32034492388">https://github.com/fosslinux/live-bootstrap/actions/runs/11507728726/job/32034492388</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="235541"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#235541" label="[23:55:41]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">don't mean to interrupt; there's another open question related to python, since i tried to statically compile/link that with tcc too</span></div><div class="line" id="235637"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#235637" label="[23:56:37]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">the python bootstrapping isn't done with tcc to my knowledge, i didn't manage to see a python-3.18 pass with tcc</span></div><div class="line" id="235653"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#235653" label="[23:56:53]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and i didn't succeed with statically linking python with gcc/binutils either</span></div><div class="line" id="235754"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#235754" label="[23:57:54]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">question is, if i had missed anything, because i can't keep python self-hosting with tcc/static-linking, hence will loose portage</span></div><div class="line" id="235917"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#235917" label="[23:59:17]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">far less critical issue than the perl one, to keep autotools instead of rewriting hundreds of configure.ac/makefile.am</span></div><br /></div></body></html>